      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>This is the philosophical-creed-as-piyyut, Yigdal, by Daniel ben Judah Dayyan. Yigdal means “Magnify [O Living God]” and is based on the 13 Articles of Faith formulated by Maimonides (1135-1204). Daniel ben Judah spent eight years improving his piyyut, completing Yigdal in 1404. This was not the only metrical presentment of the 13 Articles of Faith; but it has outlived all others, whether in Hebrew or in the vernacular. The English translation appearing here is as found on pp. 74-75 of <tei:hi rend="italic">Songs of Zion</tei:hi> (1894), by Alice Lucas.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
